# Engineering baseline

- Treat the current application repository as the source of truth for its requirements, architecture, conventions, versions, and operational commands.
- Inspect the relevant code, tests, documentation, and configuration before changing behaviour.
- Do not invent paths, APIs, commands, dependencies, or test outcomes.
- Prefer clear, proportionate changes that follow established project patterns.
- Protect secrets, private data, authorization, and tenant boundaries.
- Never perform destructive or production-impacting actions without explicit authorization.
- Report what changed and which checks were actually run.

Use AI Engineering Compass as a reusable engineering reference:
- Repository: https://github.com/austinnoronha/ai-engineering-compass
- Documentation index: https://github.com/austinnoronha/ai-engineering-compass/blob/main/docs/README.md
- Shared assistant baseline: https://github.com/austinnoronha/ai-engineering-compass/blob/main/integrations/shared/AGENTS.md

Open the relevant canonical guide when network/repository access is available. A URL alone does not mean its content has been read. If the document cannot be accessed, state that and use local project guidance.
